(Before vectorization, raw input strings undergo deterministic natural language cleaning:) Tj
T* (1. Case Normalization: Strings are converted entirely to lower-case characters.) Tj
T* (2. Regex Punctuation Stripping: All symbols, punctuation marks, currency symbols, and extra whitespace are) Tj
T* (removed using regex pattern [^a-z0-9\\s].) Tj
T* (3. Tokenization: Text is split on whitespace boundaries into an array of unigrams and bi-grams.) Tj
T* (4. Stopword Filtering: Non-informative grammatical tokens \("the", "and", "at", "for", "in", "to", "from", "with",) Tj
T* ("on"\) are removed using an optimized hash set.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 621.9214960629921052 Td
(6.2 TF-IDF Feature Engineering Formulation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.122 0.161 0.216 rg
56.6929133858267775 604.9136220472440755 Td
(Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency \(TF-IDF\) converts textual sequences into numerical feature) Tj
T* (vectors that reflect the relative importance of a term within a specific document and across the entire corpus:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (• Sublinear Term Frequency: Rather than raw occurrence count, sublinear scaling is applied to prevent) Tj
T* (high-frequency words from dominating the gradient:) Tj
T* (    TF\(t, d\) = 1 + ln\(count\(t, d\)\)  if count > 0, else 0) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (• Smooth Inverse Document Frequency: Penalizes ubiquitous words across categories:) Tj
T* (    IDF\(t, D\) = ln\(\(1 + N\) / \(1 + DF\(t\)\)\) + 1) Tj
T* (    where N is total training corpus size \(600\) and DF\(t\) is number of documents containing term t.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (• Euclidean L2 Vector Normalization: Ensures that longer expense descriptions do not produce artificially) Tj
T* (inflated vector magnitudes:) Tj
T* (    v_norm = v / ||v||_2) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 403.0868503937006722 Td
(6.3 Stratified Train/Test Dataset Split) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.122 0.161 0.216 rg
56.6929133858267775 386.0789763779526425 Td
(To guarantee an honest and technically rigorous evaluation, the verified 600-sample dataset was partitioned) Tj
T* (using a Stratified 80/20 Train/Test Split:) Tj
T* (• Training Partition \(80%\): 480 examples \(exactly 60 samples per class across all 8 categories\).) Tj
T* (• Holdout Test Partition \(20%\): 120 unseen examples \(exactly 15 samples per class across all 8 categories\).) Tj
T* (• Deterministic Pseudo-Random Seed: A reproducible linear congruential shuffle seed was utilized,) Tj
T* (guaranteeing that both the Logistic Regression and Neural Network models are evaluated on the exact) Tj
T* (identical test instances.) Tj
