(6.4 Mathematical Formulation & Softmax Activation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.122 0.161 0.216 rg
56.6929133858267775 728.5041732283464171 Td
(Multiclass Logistic Regression \(Multinomial Softmax Classifier\) serves as the industry standard baseline for) Tj
T* (text categorization tasks. Given an input feature vector x in R^D \(where D = 580 vocabulary dimensions\), the) Tj
T* (model computes linear logits for each of the K = 8 classes:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    z_k = W_k · x + b_k    for k in {1, 2, ..., K}) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (These linear logits are transformed into a normalized probabilistic distribution over classes via the Softmax) Tj
T* (function:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    P\(y = k | x\) = exp\(z_k\) / sum_{j=1}^K exp\(z_j\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 581.1025984251967884 Td
(6.5 Objective Loss Function with L2 Weight Regularization) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.122 0.161 0.216 rg
56.6929133858267775 564.0947244094487587 Td
(The model is trained by minimizing the Categorical Cross-Entropy loss augmented with an L2 Ridge penalty) Tj
T* (\(lambda = 0.0001\) to discourage weight explosion and mitigate overfitting on sparse vocabulary:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (    J\(W, b\) = - \(1 / M\) * sum_{i=1}^M ln\(P\(y^\(i\) | x^\(i\)\)\) + \(lambda / 2\) * ||W||_2^2) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (where M is the mini-batch size \(32\) and y^\(i\) is the true category label index.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11.5 Tf
13.2249999999999996 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 471.1183464566928478 Td
(6.6 Optimization: Mini-Batch Gradient Descent with Momentum & Sparse Speedup) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.122 0.161 0.216 rg
56.6929133858267775 454.1104724409448181 Td
(To achieve instant in-browser convergence without blocking the JavaScript main thread:) Tj
T* (• Momentum \(beta = 0.9\): Velocity buffers accumulate previous gradient trajectories, accelerating traversal) Tj
T* (through low-curvature regions and dampening high-frequency oscillations.) Tj
T* (• Learning Rate Schedule: Step decay learning rate starting at eta_0 = 1.2, scaled as eta_epoch = eta_0 / \(1) Tj
T* (+ 0.01 * epoch\).) Tj
T* (• Sparse Dot Product Acceleration: Because TF-IDF vectors for short descriptions contain fewer than 5) Tj
T* (non-zero entries out of 580 dimensions, a specialized sparse index iterator was engineered. Rather than) Tj
T* (computing 580 multiplications per class, the dot product only evaluates non-zero elements. This yielded a) Tj
T* (140x computational speedup, reducing full 50-epoch training time from 3.2 seconds down to 22 milliseconds.) Tj
ET
